<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/CMMN/20151109/MODEL" xmlns:cmmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/CMMN/20151109/CMMNDI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/CMMN/20151109/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/CMMN/20151109/DI" id="defs_Measurement_anomaly" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <case id="Measurement_anomaly" name="6.5.4 Investigate measurement anomalies">
    <caseFileModel id="Measurement_anomaly_cfm">
      <caseFileItem id="cf_anomaly" name="The anomaly, the read and its history"/>
      <caseFileItem id="cf_device" name="Meter, register and communication path evidence"/>
      <caseFileItem id="cf_premise" name="Premise, account and known changes of use"/>
    </caseFileModel>
    <casePlanModel id="Measurement_anomaly_plan" name="6.5.4 Investigate measurement anomalies" autoComplete="true">
      <documentation>A consumption that does not fit its context has four common causes - the meter, the communication path, the customer's actual usage, and interference - and they present identically. The order in which an analyst tests them depends on what history is available. That is the CMMN test.

THE CASE MUST BE ABLE TO END IN 'NOTHING IS WRONG'. A premise that became vacant, a seasonal change, a new appliance or a genuine change of use all produce exactly the anomaly signature this case opens on, and closing with no fault found is a correct outcome that should be recorded as one - otherwise the same premise is investigated every quarter.

Where interference is suspected the case STOPS and hands to 6.6.1. It does not investigate theft itself, because the evidence handling is different: 6.6.2 is a controlled investigation with a chain of custody, and an analyst who has already corrected the data has disturbed it.</documentation>
      <planItem id="pi_t_history" name="Review the anomaly against available history" definitionRef="t_history_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_history">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_history"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></requiredRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_device" name="Check device and register evidence" definitionRef="t_device_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_device">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_device"><condition><![CDATA[false]]></condition></requiredRule>
          <manualActivationRule id="mar_t_device"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></manualActivationRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_comms" name="Check the communication path" definitionRef="t_comms_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_comms">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_comms"><condition><![CDATA[false]]></condition></requiredRule>
          <manualActivationRule id="mar_t_comms"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></manualActivationRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_premise" name="Check premise and account context" definitionRef="t_premise_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_premise">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_premise"><condition><![CDATA[false]]></condition></requiredRule>
          <manualActivationRule id="mar_t_premise"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></manualActivationRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_field" name="Raise field evidence work" definitionRef="t_field_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_field">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_field"><condition><![CDATA[false]]></condition></requiredRule>
          <manualActivationRule id="mar_t_field"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></manualActivationRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_tamper" name="Hand to 6.6.1 where interference is suspected" definitionRef="t_tamper_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_tamper">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_tamper"><condition><![CDATA[false]]></condition></requiredRule>
          <manualActivationRule id="mar_t_tamper"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></manualActivationRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_correct" name="Correct the data where authorised" definitionRef="t_correct_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_correct">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_correct"><condition><![CDATA[false]]></condition></requiredRule>
          <manualActivationRule id="mar_t_correct"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></manualActivationRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_t_classify" name="Classify the cause and close" definitionRef="t_classify_def">
        <itemControl id="ic_t_classify">
          <requiredRule id="rr_t_classify"><condition><![CDATA[true]]></condition></requiredRule>
        </itemControl>
      </planItem>
      <planItem id="pi_m_cause" name="Cause classified" definitionRef="m_cause_def"/>
      <planItem id="pi_m_settled" name="Data settled" definitionRef="m_settled_def"/>
      <humanTask id="t_history_def" name="Review the anomaly against available history" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Required. Most anomalies resolve here, and the ones that do not are the ones worth a field visit.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_device_def" name="Check device and register evidence" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Discretionary. A failing register produces a plausible-looking drift that history alone will not separate from a change of use.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_comms_def" name="Check the communication path" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Discretionary. A path fault produces missing intervals that can look like reduced consumption - and 6.3.4's acceptance record says whether the path ever worked.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_premise_def" name="Check premise and account context" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Discretionary. Vacancy, seasonality, a new appliance, a change of use - 10.1 and 10.5 hold what changed.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_field_def" name="Raise field evidence work" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Discretionary. Through 6.2.4 where the question can only be answered at the meter.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_tamper_def" name="Hand to 6.6.1 where interference is suspected" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Discretionary in principle, decisive in effect: this case STOPS at that point. 6.6.2 runs a controlled investigation with a chain of custody, and an analyst who has already corrected the data has disturbed the evidence.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_correct_def" name="Correct the data where authorised" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Discretionary, and never where a tamper referral has been made.</documentation></humanTask>
      <humanTask id="t_classify_def" name="Classify the cause and close" isBlocking="true"><documentation>Required, INCLUDING no fault found. An unclosed anomaly is investigated again next quarter on the same premise.</documentation></humanTask>
      <milestone id="m_cause_def" name="Cause classified"><documentation>Device, communication, genuine consumption, or referred as suspected interference.</documentation></milestone>
      <milestone id="m_settled_def" name="Data settled"><documentation>Corrected, estimated, accepted as genuine, or held pending 6.6.2.</documentation></milestone>
    </casePlanModel>
  </case>
  <cmmndi:CMMNDI>
    <cmmndi:CMMNDiagram id="dg_Measurement_anomaly">
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_plan" cmmnElementRef="Measurement_anomaly_plan"><dc:Bounds x="40" y="40" width="1010" height="300"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_history" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_history"><dc:Bounds x="80" y="90" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_device" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_device"><dc:Bounds x="270" y="90" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_comms" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_comms"><dc:Bounds x="460" y="90" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_premise" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_premise"><dc:Bounds x="80" y="190" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_field" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_field"><dc:Bounds x="270" y="190" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_tamper" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_tamper"><dc:Bounds x="460" y="190" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_correct" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_correct"><dc:Bounds x="80" y="290" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_t_classify" cmmnElementRef="pi_t_classify"><dc:Bounds x="270" y="290" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_m_cause" cmmnElementRef="pi_m_cause"><dc:Bounds x="460" y="290" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
      <cmmndi:CMMNShape id="sh_pi_m_settled" cmmnElementRef="pi_m_settled"><dc:Bounds x="80" y="390" width="150" height="60"/><cmmndi:CMMNLabel/></cmmndi:CMMNShape>
    </cmmndi:CMMNDiagram>
  </cmmndi:CMMNDI>
</definitions>
